IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lss-dates`
IMPORT `lss-core`
IMPORT `lss-seat`

-- Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) -- cases for the injured person's seat (lss-seat.l4),
-- with a few on the lss-dates.l4 and lss-core.l4 functions the seat composes. Every expected value was worked by hand
-- from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), never copied from the encoding's output. Edges: the
-- commencement day and the day before; the last day of each period and the day after; 29 February; a leap-year
-- February in a 28-day count; each limb of ss 24, 27, 28 in turn; age 17 and 18 (s 3(1) "child").
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the injured person`

§§ `s 5: does the Act apply`

`applies a` MEANS `yes: the Act applies to an injury from an accident on or after 1 July 2014, whoever was at fault, even if you were (s 5(1)(a), (2))`
`applies b` MEANS `yes: the accident was before 1 July 2014, but you have been accepted into the Scheme under s 6, so the Act applies (s 5(1)(b), (2))`
`not applies` MEANS `no: the Act applies to an injury from an accident before 1 July 2014 only where the injured person is accepted into the Scheme under s 6 (s 5(1)(b))`

-- The commencement day, 1 July 2014, and the day before.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` (`the date` 1 7 2014) FALSE EQUALS `applies a`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` (`the date` 30 6 2014) FALSE EQUALS `not applies`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` (`the date` 30 6 2014) TRUE EQUALS `applies b`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` (`the date` 15 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS `applies a`

§§ `s 24 and s 55: eligibility`

`life` MEANS `the injury meets the LSS Rules' criteria for lifetime participation`
`interim only` MEANS `the injury meets the LSS Rules' criteria for interim participation only`
`neither` MEANS `the injury meets neither`
`after` MEANS `the date` 15 3 2022
`before` MEANS `the date` 15 3 2013

`e s55` MEANS `yes: under an agreement between the Authority and a prescribed authority, no other eligibility requirement applies and you are eligible for the services the agreement contemplates (s 55(2)(a), (b))`
`e s5` MEANS `no: the Act does not apply to an injury from an accident before 1 July 2014 unless you are accepted into the Scheme under s 6 (s 5(1))`
`e a` MEANS `no: a person is eligible only if they suffer a bodily injury (s 24(1)(a))`
`e b` MEANS `no: a person is eligible only if the injury was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 24(1)(b))`
`e c` MEANS `no: a person is eligible only if the accident occurred in South Australia (s 24(1)(c))`
`e race` MEANS `no: the Act's coverage is excluded for a motor vehicle injury suffered by a participant in a road race (s 24(1)(d), (5)(a))`
`e work` MEANS `no: the Act's coverage is excluded for a motor vehicle injury that is also a work injury under the Return to Work Act 2014 (s 24(1)(d), (5)(b))`
`e e` MEANS `no: a person is eligible only if the injury satisfies the LSS Rules' criteria for eligibility (s 24(1)(e))`
`e damages` MEANS `no: a person who has been awarded damages for the future treatment, care and support needs that relate to the injury, by a final judgment or a binding settlement, is not eligible (s 24(3))`
`e life` MEANS `yes: you are eligible to be a lifetime participant in the Scheme (s 24(1), (2))`
`e interim` MEANS `yes: you are eligible to be an interim participant in the Scheme (s 24(1), (2))`

-- Every limb met: lifetime, then interim.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `life` FALSE EQUALS `e life`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `interim only` FALSE EQUALS `e interim`
-- Each limb failing in turn.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `life` FALSE EQUALS `e a`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `life` FALSE EQUALS `e b`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `life` FALSE EQUALS `e c`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `life` FALSE EQUALS `e race`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `life` FALSE EQUALS `e work`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `neither` FALSE EQUALS `e e`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `life` TRUE EQUALS `e damages`
-- s 24(4): the damages bar does not apply to a person who has applied under s 6.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `before` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `life` TRUE EQUALS `e life`
-- s 5(1): a pre-commencement accident without a s 6 application.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `before` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `life` FALSE EQUALS `e s5`
-- s 55(2)(a): an agreement displaces every other requirement, including the work injury exclusion (s 24(5)(b)).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` TRUE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `neither` FALSE EQUALS `e s55`
-- A road race outside South Australia: (c) is reached first.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` FALSE `after` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `life` FALSE EQUALS `e c`

§§ `s 6: buying in`

`b not needed` MEANS `not needed: the accident was on or after 1 July 2014, so the Act applies without buying in; apply under s 25 (s 5(1)(a))`
`b insurer` MEANS `no: an application for a pre-commencement injury cannot be made by an insurer (s 6(3))`
`b person` MEANS `no: s 6(1)(a) requires the injured person to make the application`
`b a` MEANS `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have applied to the Authority in the manner and form it determines (s 6(1)(a))`
`b b` MEANS `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have given the information the Authority requires (s 6(1)(b))`
`b c` MEANS `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only if the Authority determines that it will accept you; that is the Authority's decision (s 6(1)(c))`
`b d` MEANS `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have paid the contribution the Authority determines into the Fund (s 6(1)(d))`
`b yes` MEANS `yes: you may be accepted into the Scheme as a lifetime participant (s 6(1), (2))`

#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` (`the date` 30 6 2014) `the injured person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `b yes`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` (`the date` 1 7 2014) `the injured person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `b not needed`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` `before` `an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `b insurer`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` `before` `the nominal defendant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `b person`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` `before` `someone else` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `b person`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` `before` `a person with lawful authority to act for the injured person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `b yes`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` `before` `the injured person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `b a`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` `before` `the injured person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `b b`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` `before` `the injured person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `b c`
#ASSERT `Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` `before` `the injured person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `b d`

§§ `s 25 and s 6(3): who may apply`

#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `after` `the injured person` EQUALS `yes: you may apply yourself (s 25(1)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `after` `a person with lawful authority to act for the injured person` EQUALS `yes: a person with lawful authority to act on your behalf may apply (s 25(1)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `after` `an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident` EQUALS `yes: an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident may apply, and does not need your consent (s 25(1)(b)(ii), (2))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `after` `the nominal defendant` EQUALS `yes: the nominal defendant may apply, and does not need your consent (s 25(1)(b)(iii), (2))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `after` `someone else` EQUALS `no: an application may only be made by the injured person, a person with lawful authority to act for them, an insurer of a motor vehicle involved, or the nominal defendant (s 25(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `before` `the injured person` EQUALS `yes, under s 6: for an accident before 1 July 2014, you may apply yourself (s 6(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `before` `a person with lawful authority to act for the injured person` EQUALS `yes, under s 6: for an accident before 1 July 2014, a person with lawful authority to act for you may apply on your behalf (s 6(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `before` `an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident` EQUALS `no: for an accident before 1 July 2014, an application cannot be made by an insurer (s 6(3))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` `before` `the nominal defendant` EQUALS `no: for an accident before 1 July 2014, s 6(1)(a) requires the injured person to make the application`
-- The commencement day itself is not "before" it.
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` (`the date` 1 7 2014) `the nominal defendant` EQUALS `yes: the nominal defendant may apply, and does not need your consent (s 25(1)(b)(iii), (2))`

§§ `s 25(7), s 26(10): the period the Act guarantees for applying`

-- 15 March 2022 plus 3 years is 15 March 2025 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `By when does the Act guarantee I can apply to join the Scheme` (`the date` 15 3 2022) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the date` 15 3 2025
-- 29 February 2016 plus 3 years: 28 February 2019 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `By when does the Act guarantee I can apply to join the Scheme` (`the date` 29 2 2016) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2019
-- Interim participation 1 April 2022 to 31 March 2023 is 365 days (both counted, fork F2); 15 March 2025 plus 365 days is 15 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By when does the Act guarantee I can apply to join the Scheme` (`the date` 15 3 2022) TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2022) (`the date` 31 3 2023) EQUALS `the date` 15 3 2026
-- Interim participation 1 to 10 January 2023 is 10 days; 31 August 2023 plus 10 days is 10 September 2023.
#ASSERT `By when does the Act guarantee I can apply to join the Scheme` (`the date` 31 8 2020) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2023) (`the date` 10 1 2023) EQUALS `the date` 10 9 2023
-- A one-day interim participation adds one day.
#ASSERT `By when does the Act guarantee I can apply to join the Scheme` (`the date` 15 3 2022) TRUE (`the date` 5 5 2022) (`the date` 5 5 2022) EQUALS `the date` 16 3 2025

`p yes` MEANS `yes: the application is within the 3 years from the accident that the LSS Rules must at least permit (s 25(7))`
`p interim` MEANS `yes, on fork F11: the Act fixes only the 3 years for an initial application (s 25(7)) and requires the LSS Rules to add your interim participation to whatever period they set for a lifetime application (s 26(10)); taking that period to be at least the 3 years, your application is within it`
`p rules` MEANS `not covered: the application is after the period the Act guarantees; whether it may still be made depends on the LSS Rules, which may allow a longer period (s 25(6), (7))`

#ASSERT `Is my application within the time the Act guarantees` (`the date` 15 3 2022) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `p yes`
#ASSERT `Is my application within the time the Act guarantees` (`the date` 15 3 2022) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 16 3 2025) EQUALS `p rules`
#ASSERT `Is my application within the time the Act guarantees` (`the date` 15 3 2022) TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2022) (`the date` 31 3 2023) (`the date` 16 3 2025) EQUALS `p interim`
#ASSERT `Is my application within the time the Act guarantees` (`the date` 15 3 2022) TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2022) (`the date` 31 3 2023) (`the date` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `p interim`
#ASSERT `Is my application within the time the Act guarantees` (`the date` 15 3 2022) TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2022) (`the date` 31 3 2023) (`the date` 16 3 2026) EQUALS `p rules`
#ASSERT `Is my application within the time the Act guarantees` (`the date` 15 3 2022) TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2022) (`the date` 31 3 2023) (`the date` 1 6 2023) EQUALS `p yes`

§§ `s 26(11): the limitation period with interim participation added`

-- Accrued 10 May 2020; 3 years to 10 May 2023; interim 1 to 30 June 2020 is 30 days; 10 May 2023 plus 30 is 9 June 2023.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my damages action, with my interim participation added` (`the date` 10 5 2020) (`the date` 1 6 2020) (`the date` 30 6 2020) EQUALS `the date` 9 6 2023
-- Accrued 29 February 2020; 3 years to 28 February 2023 (fork F1); interim 1 to 2 March 2020 is 2 days: 2 March 2023.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my damages action, with my interim participation added` (`the date` 29 2 2020) (`the date` 1 3 2020) (`the date` 2 3 2020) EQUALS `the date` 2 3 2023

§§ `s 26: acceptance`

#ASSERT `Must the Authority accept me as a participant` TRUE `lifetime participation` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant (s 26(2), (3)(a)), and you then remain a participant for life (s 26(5))`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority accept me as a participant` TRUE `interim participation` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Authority must accept you as an interim participant (s 26(2), (3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority accept me as a participant` FALSE `lifetime participation` TRUE EQUALS `no: the Authority is not bound to accept you unless it is satisfied that you are eligible; and you become a participant only if it is satisfied of that and accepts you in writing (s 26(1), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority accept me as a participant` TRUE `interim participation` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Authority is not bound to accept you until it is satisfied that the application was duly made (s 26(2)(b)); it may still accept you if it is satisfied that you are eligible (s 26(1))`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority accept me as a participant` FALSE `interim participation` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Authority is not bound to accept you unless it is satisfied that you are eligible; and you become a participant only if it is satisfied of that and accepts you in writing (s 26(1), (2)(a))`

#ASSERT `Must I be accepted as a lifetime participant` `a lifetime participant` FALSE EQUALS `already: a lifetime participant remains a participant for life (s 26(5))`
#ASSERT `Must I be accepted as a lifetime participant` `an interim participant` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant (s 26(4)); you then cease to be an interim participant and remain a participant for life (s 26(9))`
#ASSERT `Must I be accepted as a lifetime participant` `an interim participant` FALSE EQUALS `no, not yet: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant only once it becomes satisfied, during your interim participation, that you are eligible for lifetime participation; the decision should be made at an appropriate time after your injury has stabilised (s 26(4), (6))`
#ASSERT `Must I be accepted as a lifetime participant` `a person whose interim participation has ended under the LSS Rules` TRUE EQUALS `not by s 26(4), which speaks of satisfaction during interim participation; but the end of your interim participation does not prevent your later acceptance as a lifetime participant (s 26(8))`

§§ `ss 4, 27, 28: payment`

-- Argument order: participant, suspended, kind, declared excluded, assessed, excluded from s 27, necessary and
-- reasonable, gratuitous, age, ordinary cost of a child, approved provider required, approved, medical practitioner,
-- LSS Rules allow, contravention, within limits.
`pay yes` MEANS `yes: the Authority is to pay the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`

#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `attendant care and support services` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `pay yes`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` FALSE FALSE `attendant care and support services` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the Authority pays only for expenses incurred while you are a participant in the Scheme (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE TRUE `attendant care and support services` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the Authority is not required to pay for anything provided while your participation is suspended (s 28(6))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `another kind` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: it is not a treatment, care and support need within s 4(1), and the Authority has not determined it to be one (s 4(1)(m))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `aids and appliances` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the LSS Rules declare it an excluded treatment, care and support need, and the Authority is not liable for it (ss 4(2), 27(3)(a))`
-- s 4(2) is subject to s 4(1)(m): an LSS Rules exclusion does not reach a need the Authority determined (fork F5).
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `another kind the Authority has determined, generally or for you` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `pay yes`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `prostheses` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the Authority is not liable for a need that is not an assessed treatment, care and support need (s 27(2), (3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `prostheses` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the LSS Rules exclude it from the operation of s 27, and the Authority is not liable for it (s 27(3)(c))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `prostheses` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: the Authority pays only the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `respite care` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not required: it was provided gratuitously (s 28(1)(a)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
-- s 3(1) "child": under 18. At 17 the ordinary costs of raising a child are not required; at 18 they are paid.
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `education and vocational training` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 17 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not required: for a child, it falls within the ordinary costs of raising a child (s 28(1)(b), (7)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `education and vocational training` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 18 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `pay yes`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `education and vocational training` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `pay yes`
-- s 28(1)(c) and (4).
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `rehabilitation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not required: it must be provided by an approved provider and the provider was not approved at the time (s 28(1)(c)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `rehabilitation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `pay yes`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `medical treatment, including pharmaceuticals` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `pay yes`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `rehabilitation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `pay yes`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `home and transport modification` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not required: it was provided in contravention of the LSS Rules (s 28(1)(d)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
#ASSERT `Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` TRUE FALSE `home and transport modification` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, but only up to the limit the LSS Rules place on it (s 27(1), (4)(b))`

§§ `ss 39 to 41: rates`

`r bulk` MEANS `at the rate the bulk billing arrangement provides (s 39(2))`
`r gazette` MEANS `at the rate the Minister for Health determines by order published in the Gazette (s 40(2)(a))`
`r max 40` MEANS `at the maximum rate fixed by notice in the Gazette, which is the most the Authority is liable for (ss 40(2)(b), 41(3), (5))`
`r customary` MEANS `at the rate reasonably appropriate to the treatment or service, having regard to the customary charge made in the community for it (s 40(2)(c))`
`r max 41` MEANS `at most the maximum amount fixed by notice in the Gazette (s 41(3), (5))`
`r none` MEANS `not covered: ss 40 and 41 set no rate for it; the Authority pays the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`

#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `treatment at a public hospital` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `r bulk`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `treatment at a public hospital` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r gazette`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `conveying by ambulance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r customary`
-- s 41(1)(e): the Minister may bring ambulance within s 41 by Gazette notice; s 40(2)(b) then applies.
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `conveying by ambulance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r max 40`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `medical treatment elsewhere than at a public hospital` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r max 40`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `dental treatment elsewhere than at a public hospital` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r customary`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `rehabilitation services elsewhere than at a public hospital` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r max 40`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `attendant care and support services` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r max 41`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `attendant care and support services` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r none`
-- Treatment at a private hospital is medical treatment within s 40(1)(c): s 40(2)(b) with a maximum, s 40(2)(c) without.
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `treatment at a private hospital` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r max 40`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `treatment at a private hospital` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `r customary`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `a service the Minister has identified for s 41 by notice in the Gazette` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r max 41`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `another service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `r none`
#ASSERT `At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` `another service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `r bulk`

§§ `s 31: cooperation`

#ASSERT `Must I comply with this request for my needs assessment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you must comply with a reasonable request made in connection with the assessment of your needs, including a request to undergo an examination (s 31); if the LSS Rules so provide, failing to comply with a requirement for the assessment can lead to the suspension of your participation (s 32(2)(e))`
#ASSERT `Must I comply with this request for my needs assessment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: s 31 requires you to comply only with a reasonable request`
#ASSERT `Must I comply with this request for my needs assessment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: s 31 applies to requests by the Authority or an assessor in connection with an assessment of your treatment, care and support needs`
#ASSERT `Must I comply with this request for my needs assessment` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: s 31 binds participants in the Scheme`

§§ `Part 5: review routes and costs`

`officer` MEANS `a review officer first: you may apply to have the dispute reviewed by a review officer (s 34(1)); then, as a party, you may apply to the Tribunal within 28 days of the review officer's determination (s 35)`
`panel` MEANS `an expert review panel: the dispute may be referred to a panel by notice given to the Authority by you or on your behalf (s 36(1), (2)(b)(i)); if the panel determines that you are ineligible or do not qualify, you may apply to the Tribunal within 28 days of its determination (s 37)`

#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `whether I suffered a bodily injury` FALSE EQUALS `officer`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `whether the incident was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle` FALSE EQUALS `officer`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `whether the accident occurred in South Australia` FALSE EQUALS `officer`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `whether the Act's coverage is excluded because of a road race or a work injury` FALSE EQUALS `officer`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `whether my application was made within the period the LSS Rules specify` FALSE EQUALS `officer`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `a determination that suspends my participation` TRUE EQUALS `officer`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `whether my injury resulted from the accident or from some other condition, event or factor` FALSE EQUALS `panel`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `whether my injury satisfies the LSS Rules' criteria for eligibility` FALSE EQUALS `panel`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `how two or more of my injuries are related` TRUE EQUALS `panel`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `whether my injury is within or excluded from the coverage of the Act under the LSS Rules` TRUE EQUALS `panel`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `the assessment of my treatment, care and support needs` TRUE EQUALS `an expert review panel review of the assessment: apply within 28 days after you are given notice of the assessment, unless the LSS Rules allow more time; the panel's decision is final and binding for the purposes of the Act, though not against judicial review (s 38)`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `the assessment of my treatment, care and support needs` FALSE EQUALS `not covered: s 38 lets a participant in the Scheme apply for review of an assessment`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `another decision` TRUE EQUALS `not covered: Part 5 provides no review of this decision; the Authority's code of conduct must include a process for complaints about how it exercised a function or power (s 23(2)(a))`

`c own` MEANS `yes: the Authority pays the costs of the proceedings, including your necessary travel and accommodation costs in attending (ss 34(9), (10)(a), 36(5), (6)(a), 38(10), (11)(a))`
`c carer` MEANS `yes: the Authority pays the costs of the proceedings, including the necessary travel and accommodation costs of a carer (who may be a parent) who accompanies and supports you (ss 34(10)(a), 36(6)(a), 38(11)(a))`
`c other` MEANS `yes: the costs of the proceedings are payable by the Authority (ss 34(9), 36(5), 38(10))`
`c rep` MEANS `no: the costs the Authority pays do not include any costs of being represented (ss 34(10)(b)(i), 36(6)(b)(i), 38(11)(b)(i))`
`c unnecessary` MEANS `not covered: travel and accommodation costs are included only so far as they are necessary (ss 34(10)(a), 36(6)(a), 38(11)(a))`
`c tribunal` MEANS `not covered: the Act says nothing of costs before the Tribunal`

#ASSERT `Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` `a review officer (s 34)` `my travel and accommodation to attend` TRUE EQUALS `c own`
#ASSERT `Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` `a review officer (s 34)` `my travel and accommodation to attend` FALSE EQUALS `c unnecessary`
#ASSERT `Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` `an expert review panel on an eligibility dispute (s 36)` `the travel and accommodation of a carer who accompanies and supports me` TRUE EQUALS `c carer`
#ASSERT `Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` `an expert review panel reviewing my needs assessment (s 38)` `the travel and accommodation of a carer who accompanies and supports me` FALSE EQUALS `c unnecessary`
#ASSERT `Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` `an expert review panel reviewing my needs assessment (s 38)` `the cost of being represented` TRUE EQUALS `c rep`
#ASSERT `Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` `a review officer (s 34)` `the cost of being represented` TRUE EQUALS `c rep`
#ASSERT `Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` `an expert review panel on an eligibility dispute (s 36)` `another cost of the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS `c other`
#ASSERT `Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` `the Tribunal (ss 35, 37)` `my travel and accommodation to attend` TRUE EQUALS `c tribunal`

§§ `ss 35(2), 37(3): the Tribunal, 28 days (regulative rule)`

-- 5 February 2024 plus 28 days is 4 March 2024 (2024 is a leap year: 24 days to 29 February, then 4).
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to the Tribunal` (`the date` 5 2 2024) EQUALS `the date` 4 3 2024
-- 10 January 2025 plus 28 days is 7 February 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to the Tribunal` (`the date` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `the date` 7 2 2025

`t officer` MEANS `review of a review officer's determination (s 35)`
`t panel` MEANS `review of an expert review panel's determination that I am ineligible or do not qualify (s 37)`
`t in` MEANS `in time: the application was made within 28 days of the date of the determination (ss 35(2), 37(3))`
`t still` MEANS `still in time: you may apply to the Tribunal, within 28 days of the date of the determination (ss 35(2), 37(3))`
`t late` MEANS `no: an application for review must be made within 28 days of the date of the determination, and that time has passed (ss 35(2), 37(3))`

-- The last day and the day after, applied and not yet applied.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` `t officer` TRUE (`the date` 5 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 4 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) EQUALS `t in`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` `t officer` TRUE (`the date` 5 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 5 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) EQUALS `t late`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` `t panel` FALSE (`the date` 5 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 6 2 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) EQUALS `t in`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` `t panel` FALSE (`the date` 5 2 2024) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 4 3 2024) EQUALS `t still`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` `t panel` FALSE (`the date` 5 2 2024) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 5 3 2024) EQUALS `t late`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` `t officer` TRUE (`the date` 10 1 2025) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 7 2 2025) EQUALS `t still`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` `t officer` TRUE (`the date` 10 1 2025) TRUE (`the date` 8 2 2025) (`the date` 8 2 2025) EQUALS `t late`
-- s 35 is for a party to the dispute.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` `t officer` FALSE (`the date` 5 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 6 2 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) EQUALS `not covered: s 35 lets a party to the dispute apply to the Tribunal`

§§ `s 38(3): review of the assessment, 28 days (regulative rule)`

-- 20 December 2024 plus 28 days is 17 January 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for review of my needs assessment` (`the date` 20 12 2024) EQUALS `the date` 17 1 2025

`a in` MEANS `in time: the application was made within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment (s 38(3))`
`a still` MEANS `still in time: you may apply, within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment (s 38(3))`
`a ext` MEANS `the LSS Rules' extension governs: the 28 days do not apply where an extension of time is allowed under the LSS Rules (s 38(3))`
`a late` MEANS `no: the application must be made within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment, that time has passed, and no extension has been allowed under the LSS Rules (s 38(3))`

#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for review of my needs assessment` TRUE (`the date` 20 12 2024) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 17 1 2025) (`the date` 1 2 2025) EQUALS `a in`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for review of my needs assessment` TRUE (`the date` 20 12 2024) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 18 1 2025) (`the date` 1 2 2025) EQUALS `a late`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for review of my needs assessment` TRUE (`the date` 20 12 2024) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 18 1 2025) (`the date` 1 2 2025) EQUALS `a ext`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for review of my needs assessment` TRUE (`the date` 20 12 2024) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 17 1 2025) EQUALS `a still`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for review of my needs assessment` TRUE (`the date` 20 12 2024) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 18 1 2025) EQUALS `a late`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for review of my needs assessment` TRUE (`the date` 20 12 2024) TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 18 1 2025) EQUALS `a ext`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for review of my needs assessment` FALSE (`the date` 20 12 2024) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 21 12 2024) (`the date` 1 2 2025) EQUALS `not covered: s 38 lets a participant in the Scheme apply for review of an assessment`

§§ `s 52: leaving Australia, at least 28 days' notice (regulative rule)`

-- 1 March 2025 less 28 days is 1 February 2025; 1 March 2024 (a leap year) less 28 days is 2 February 2024.
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the Authority I am leaving Australia` (`the date` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `the date` 1 2 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the Authority I am leaving Australia` (`the date` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `the date` 2 2 2024

`n in` MEANS `in time: you gave notice at least 28 days before leaving (s 52(1)); the Authority may still suspend your participation while you are absent (s 52(2)(b))`
`n still` MEANS `still in time: give the Authority notice, in accordance with the LSS Rules, at least 28 days before leaving (s 52(1)); the Authority may suspend your participation while you are absent (s 52(2)(b))`
`n late` MEANS `no: notice must be given at least 28 days before leaving Australia (s 52(1)); the Authority may waive or reduce that period (s 52(2)(a)), and may suspend your participation while you are absent whether or not notice was given (s 52(2)(b))`
`n waived` MEANS `the Authority has waived or reduced the period: the 28 days do not apply to you as they stand (s 52(2)(a))`

#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 2 2025) (`the date` 10 2 2025) EQUALS `n in`
#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 2 2 2025) (`the date` 10 2 2025) EQUALS `n late`
#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 12 2024) (`the date` 10 2 2025) EQUALS `n in`
#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 2 2025) EQUALS `n still`
#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 2 2 2025) EQUALS `n late`
#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 2 2 2024) (`the date` 2 2 2024) EQUALS `n in`
#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 3 2 2024) (`the date` 3 2 2024) EQUALS `n late`
#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 25 2 2025) EQUALS `n waived`
#ASSERT `Have I given notice of my absence in time` FALSE (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 25 2 2025) EQUALS `not covered: s 52 binds participants in the Scheme`

