§§ `s 49 and Schedule 1 cl 6(7)`

#ASSERT `Can I sue the assessor, review officer or panel member personally` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: they are not personally liable for what they did or omitted in good faith in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act; the liability attaches instead to the Crown (s 49(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the assessor, review officer or panel member personally` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: s 49 protects only what was done or omitted in good faith in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the assessor, review officer or panel member personally` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: s 49 protects only what was done or omitted in good faith in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act`

#ASSERT `Can what I told the expert review panel be used in later proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: information given to an expert review panel may be used in proceedings before a court or the Tribunal (Schedule 1 cl 6(7)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can what I told the expert review panel be used in later proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: information given to an expert review panel may be used in other proceedings because you consent (Schedule 1 cl 6(7)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can what I told the expert review panel be used in later proceedings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: information given to an expert review panel cannot be used in subsequent proceedings unless they are before a court or the Tribunal, or you consent (Schedule 1 cl 6(7))`
#ASSERT `Can what I told the expert review panel be used in later proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: information given to an expert review panel may be used in proceedings before a court or the Tribunal (Schedule 1 cl 6(7)(a))`
